<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFrameworks>net8.0;net10.0</TargetFrameworks>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <LangVersion>latest</LangVersion>
    <AllowUnsafeBlocks>true</AllowUnsafeBlocks>
    
    <!-- NuGet Package Metadata -->
    <Title>EffinitiveFramework.Core</Title>
    <Authors>Henry Bartosch</Authors>
    <PackageId>EffinitiveFramework.Core</PackageId>
    <Version>2.7.1</Version>
    <RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/HBartosch/Effinitive</RepositoryUrl>
    <PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/HBartosch/Effinitive</PackageProjectUrl>
    <PackageTags>http;http2;web-framework;high-performance;zero-allocation;minimal-api;aspnetcore-alternative;hpack;alpn;tls;https;fast;low-latency;microservices;sse;server-sent-events;streaming</PackageTags>
    <Description>HTTP/1.1, HTTP/2 and HTTP/3 web framework for .NET 8+, built from scratch. Allocation-conscious routing, a custom HTTP/2 implementation with HPACK, WebSockets, TLS with per-listener ALPN and certificate rotation, response caching, rate limiting and OpenAPI generation.</Description>
    <PackageIcon>PackageIconResized.png</PackageIcon>
    <PackageLicenseFile>LICENSE</PackageLicenseFile>
    <PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
    <PackageReleaseNotes>v2.7.1: WebSocket conformance. The Autobahn TestSuite failed 110 of its 301 cases against 2.7.0; none fail now.

Every failure was a malformed frame accepted and processed as though it were valid, which a well-behaved client never sends and so nothing had noticed. RFC 6455 section 5.2 requires RSV1-3 to be zero unless a negotiated extension defines them, and reserves every opcode outside 0x0-0x2 and 0x8-0xA; both were ignored. Section 5.4 requires a continuation frame to continue something, so an orphan continuation or a data frame arriving mid-fragment is now refused. Section 5.6 requires a text message's payload to be valid UTF-8 and section 8.1 requires the connection to fail with 1007 when it is not; Encoding.UTF8 substitutes U+FFFD and reports success, so invalid input was being echoed back as though it had been understood, which was 75 of the 110 failures. Section 5.5.1 allows a close frame to carry nothing or a two-octet code and an optional reason, and section 7.4.1 reserves the codes; the payload was not read at all and the reply always said 1000 rather than echoing the peer's code.

This changes what the server accepts. A peer sending invalid UTF-8, setting a reserved bit, or closing with a reserved status code now has its connection failed where it was previously tolerated.</PackageReleaseNotes>
    <RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
    <Copyright>Copyright (c) 2025 Henry Bartosch</Copyright>
    <PackageRequireLicenseAcceptance>false</PackageRequireLicenseAcceptance>
    <GeneratePackageOnBuild>false</GeneratePackageOnBuild>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="EffinitiveFramework.Tests" />
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="EffinitiveFramework.Benchmarks" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!-- HTTP/3 (QUIC) only available on .NET 10+ -->
  <ItemGroup Condition="'$(TargetFramework)' == 'net8.0'">
    <Compile Remove="Http3\**" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.CodeAnalysis.NetAnalyzers" Version="9.0.0" Condition="'$(TargetFramework)' == 'net8.0'">
      <IncludeAssets>runtime; build; native; contentfiles; analyzers; buildtransitive</IncludeAssets>
      <PrivateAssets>all</PrivateAssets>
    </PackageReference>
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.CodeAnalysis.NetAnalyzers" Version="10.0.100" Condition="'$(TargetFramework)' == 'net10.0'">
      <IncludeAssets>runtime; build; native; contentfiles; analyzers; buildtransitive</IncludeAssets>
      <PrivateAssets>all</PrivateAssets>
    </PackageReference>
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.ObjectPool" Version="8.0.0" Condition="'$(TargetFramework)' == 'net8.0'" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.ObjectPool" Version="10.0.0" Condition="'$(TargetFramework)' == 'net10.0'" />
    <PackageReference Include="SecurityCodeScan.VS2019" Version="5.6.7">
      <IncludeAssets>runtime; build; native; contentfiles; analyzers; buildtransitive</IncludeAssets>
      <PrivateAssets>all</PrivateAssets>
    </PackageReference>
    <PackageReference Include="System.IO.Pipelines" Version="8.0.0" Condition="'$(TargetFramework)' == 'net8.0'" />
    <PackageReference Include="System.IO.Pipelines" Version="10.0.0" Condition="'$(TargetFramework)' == 'net10.0'" />
    <PackageReference Include="System.IdentityModel.Tokens.Jwt" Version="8.16.0" />
    <PackageReference Include="Routya.ResultKit" Version="2.1.0" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <None Include="..\..\LICENSE" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
    <None Include="..\..\README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
    <None Include="..\..\PackageIconResized.png" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
